h and I think whether you  say that's a libertarian or not people I  think libertarians become a better term  that once was but it still scares some  people and it's used by some people to  scare others particularly in the south  and different places people use it as a  as a weapon to try to scare people what  well I think that they're not sure what  that means what the word means although  I would say that since the the George W  Bush era when the term conservative  became somewhat meaningless that now a  lot of people and you'll see boohoo  probably really are more traditional  conservative saying wanting to use the  word libertarian because it's more  distinctive term so in some ways it has  come into better usage now in the among  the common public but I think people  understand constitutional conservative  better at least where I'm from than they  do the word libertarian but I think they  can mean somewhat the same thing now on  your bookshelf behind you I see Judge  Napolitano I see Ludwig von Mises you're  obscuring the copy of Marx back there  but who were who were your insight in  the art of a motorcycle man yeah Robert  piercing so and Flannery O'Connor this  is yeah  I you know I think that I have some one  eclectic background I like literature I  was a English minor and in school and  science because I went into medicine but  I was always a big fan of the short  story big fan of Dostoevsky as far as a  novelist goes but I read a lot of the  free market people and it was influenced  by that I met quite a few of them along  the way you know Amit Han sent Holtz  several times  Mises only had four PhDs met Murray  Rothbard through the year so you know I  was exposed to a lot of them Henry  Hazlitt you know we were talking about  getting some books for the interns you  know when they come and I thought they  should all have Henry Hazlitt second ah  mcc's in one lesson in Basquiat so the  law has two things that they leave our  office and had been here they ca