e we  have chaos and you know I'd get in  trouble on the campaign trail for  criticism I'll say I get in trouble I  don't send me to the principal's office  but I get criticism because you know I  would talk about how in when  currency was destroyed 1923 they voted  in Hitler and if I sell you're comparing  someone hey I'm not comparing anyone -  I'm just saying that in the times of  crisis  even a panicky public can vote in  someone who says give me your Liberty  and I'll give you security and I don't  want that to happen and so I think the  best way is all these things can be  gradually reformed I mean some of the  Rotarians give me a hard time because  I'm going to try to reform Social  Security rather than just privatize it  I'd love to privatize it I'd love to  have individual accounts but the first  step we're gonna do is try to fix it by  just letting the age gradually rise  means testing the benefits things that  aren't perfect libertarian utopias but  you got to fix I think some of the  entitlement programs just in order not  to face this budgetary crisis it's  coming thank you I'm Nick Gillespie for  Reason TV with Matt Welch of Reason  magazine we want to thank Senator Rand  Paul of Kentucky for taking time to talk  with us - thank you
 

